{
  "summary": "Skips the Avoid Partial Spends (APS) coin selection pass when the initial ungrouped coin selection does not leave any scriptPubKey partially spent. It tracks available and selected UTXO counts per scriptPubKey during transaction creation, returning a `has_partial_spend` flag that gates the second selection pass.",
  "problem": "The wallet unconditionally runs a second coin selection pass with APS enabled whenever fee conditions allow, even if the first selection already spent all or none of the UTXOs for each scriptPubKey. This causes redundant computation and causes USDT tracepoints and logs to falsely report that APS was used to avoid partial spends.",
  "evidence": [
    "Fixes issue #25150: 'Coin Selection tracepoint overreports use of APS'",
    "PR description: 'The second pass runs even when the first selection left no partial spend for it to avoid, and aps_create_tx_internal then reports APS as used whenever the grouped result is taken, overreporting how often a partial spend was avoided.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Modifies `CreateTransactionInternal` and `CreateTransaction` in `src/wallet/spend.cpp`, adjusting tracepoint tests and adding new wallet group functional tests.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Added explicit functional tests in `test/functional/wallet_groups.py` to verify that APS is not attempted when all scriptPubKeys hold only one UTXO, and to verify that manually preselected inputs count towards their scriptPubKey.",
  "card": "This pull request ensures the wallet only attempts a second Avoid Partial Spends (APS) coin selection pass when the initial ungrouped selection actually left a scriptPubKey partially spent. Previously, the wallet ran the APS pass whenever fee limits allowed, wasting computation during transaction creation and causing USDT tracepoints and debug logs to overreport APS usage (fixing issue #25150). The change counts selected versus available coins per scriptPubKey and updates functional tests covering USDT tracepoints and wallet input grouping.",
